// Part of the Plew compiler module (root: _.pw). Lowering reads the shared
// @Plew/Syntax `SyntaxFile` rows (expression / statement / block / pattern IDs)
// into the compiler arena (Expr / Stmt / Block / MatchArm). The compiler entry
// uses the direct SyntaxFile builder; macro-facing value parsing stays an explicit
// `parseItem` boundary and is not an ambient dependency of this module.
//
// Names: most are re-interned into c.arena.bytes (codegen `writeSpan` emits the text and
// resolution compares bytes, both of which work on a re-interned copy). The two
// names that feed `moduleOf` (cross-module visibility) keep their ORIGINAL offset:
// a `Call` name (at its node span's start) and a function *declaration* name (still
// produced by the compiler's own declaration parser, untouched here). String and
// `Ident` text also use the original span (exact bytes matter for string literals).

//
// Split across `Lower/` for readability; all parts share the module scope.

part ./Lower/Types
part ./Lower/Expr
part ./Lower/Params
part ./Lower/Registration
part ./Lower/Match
part ./Lower/Decl
part ./Lower/Impl
part ./Lower/TopLevel
